This rule applies to the **web** frontend only. The project also has a **native mobile app** (separate codebase); see .cursor/rules/12-interfaces-admin-user-mobile.mdc.

Frontend stack (FinShield AI):
- Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript 5
- Tailwind CSS 3, Zustand, TanStack Query v5, Recharts + D3.js
- Socket.IO client for real-time alerts and transaction feed
- React Hook Form + Zod, TanStack Table v8
- NextAuth.js (Azure AD provider) for auth
- Vitest, React Testing Library, Playwright for tests

Frontend rules:
- Prefer TypeScript for all frontend logic; strict types.
- Keep components small, reusable, and focused.
- Keep presentation separate from data-fetching logic (hooks, API client).
- Handle loading, error, and empty states explicitly.
- Support real-time updates (Socket.IO) for live alerts, transaction feed, and dashboard metrics.
- **Two UIs in one app:** **Admin** (e.g. `/admin/*`, settings, rules, ML models, watchlists) and **Analyst/Operator** (dashboard, transactions, fraud-alerts, cases, analytics, entities, network-graph); use role-based routing and layout; shared design system and API client.

Product-area alignment (docs/PRD.md, CLAUDE.md):
- **Admin (web only):** Rules engine, ML model registry, watchlist/sanctions config, system settings, API keys, team management, audit log.
- **Analyst/Operator (web):** Dashboard, transactions (list/detail + fraud analysis), fraud alerts (list/detail, assign, resolve, escalate), case management, risk scoring, analytics/reports, entity 360, network graph, notifications.
- **Native mobile app:** Separate codebase; not covered by this rule.

Preferred frontend structure (per CLAUDE.md):
- frontend/src/app/              (App Router: (auth), (dashboard) with dashboard/, transactions/, fraud-alerts/, risk-scoring/, analytics/, rules-engine/, case-management/, ml-models/, entities/, watchlists/, audit-log/, settings/, network-graph/)
- frontend/src/components/       (ui/, layout/, charts/, dashboard/, transactions/, fraud/, rules/, network/, shared/)
- frontend/src/hooks/, lib/, stores/, types/
- frontend/tests/unit/, e2e/

UI/UX rules:
- Accessible markup and semantic HTML.
- Reusable design system components; avoid oversized page components.
- State/data: centralized API client, normalized API patterns, careful auth state; validate critical inputs client- and server-side.

Do not:
- Mix many responsibilities into one component.
- Hardcode API URLs in components.
- Put admin-only flows in the mobile app codebase (admin is web only).
