description: Next.js frontend rules for FinShield AI
globs: frontend/**/*.ts, frontend/**/*.tsx
---

Frontend stack:
- Next.js 14 (App Router)
- React 18
- Tailwind CSS 3
- TypeScript 5
- Zustand (State Management)
- TanStack Query v5 (React Query)
- Socket.IO Client (Real-Time)
- NextAuth.js (Auth)
- Recharts + D3.js (Charts)
- React Hook Form + Zod (Forms)
- TanStack Table v8 (Tables/Data Grids)

Frontend rules:
- Strict TypeScript (no `any` unless absolutely necessary).
- Functional components only (no class components).
- Server components by default, client components only when needed (`"use client"`).
- Prefer server-side data fetching in page components.
- Use custom hooks for reusable logic.
- Colocate components with their types and tests.
- Use `cn()` utility for conditional Tailwind classes.
- Use Zod schemas that mirror backend Pydantic schemas.

Preferred frontend structure:
- `frontend/src/app/` - Next.js App Router pages and layouts
- `frontend/src/components/ui/` - Base UI primitives (Tailwind)
- `frontend/src/components/layout/` - Shell, sidebar, topbar
- `frontend/src/components/shared/` - Shared business components
- `frontend/src/hooks/` - Custom React hooks
- `frontend/src/lib/` - API clients, socket setup, utils
- `frontend/src/stores/` - Zustand stores
- `frontend/src/types/` - TypeScript interfaces and types
- `frontend/tests/` - Vitest and Playwright tests

UI/UX rules:
- Handle loading, error, and empty states explicitly.
- Use accessible markup and semantic HTML.
- Avoid oversized page components. Extract logic to hooks and UI to smaller components.

State/data rules:
- Use TanStack Query v5 for server state and caching.
- Use Zustand for global client state (e.g., UI toggles, active filters).
- Centralize API calls in `lib/api-client.ts`.
- Manage WebSockets via `hooks/use-socket.ts`.

Testing 
- Vitest (unit and integration tests)
- React Testing Library (component testing)
- Playwright (E2E tests)

Do not:
- Mix many responsibilities into one component.
- Hardcode API URLs (use `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`).
- Duplicate UI patterns that should be shared.
